<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Royal Commentaries of the Incas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1609</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Comentarios Reales de los Incas</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Comentarios Reales de los <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Incas</a> is a history of the Inca Empire by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-garcilaso-de-la-vega">Inca Garcilaso de la Vega</a>, the son of a Spanish conquistador and an Inca noblewoman, published in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisbon">Lisbon</a> in 1609, with a second part on the conquest in 1617. Drawing on his childhood in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cusco">Cusco</a> and on Spanish chroniclers, it shaped European views of the Incas for centuries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/royal-commentaries-of-the-incas.jpg" alt="Royal Commentaries of the Incas" width="320" height="452" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vega, Garcilaso de la, 1539-1616 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Garcilaso_de_la_Vega_Commentarios_Reales_1609.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
